# Allowlist: ignore everything, then re-include only what `go build ./cmd/server` and the image
# need. Anything new in the repo stays out of the build by default -- a blocklist would need
# every new file type remembered, and since the Dockerfile's `COPY . .` precedes `go build`,
# any stray file in the context busts the build cache whenever it changes.
#
# Patterns here match from the context root: `*.md` would only catch root-level files, so
# exclusions below use `**/`.
*

!go.mod
!go.sum
!config.yaml

!cmd/
!gen/
!internal/
!build/swagger/docs.go

# Inside the re-included trees: tests, examples and docs are never compiled into the server.
**/*_test.go
internal/test/
internal/hnsw/example/
internal/hnsw/.github/
**/*.md
**/LICENSE
**/.gitignore
